A DNVT ON A 64 kbps CHANNEL -- both ends on mf8.BASE, the DNVT at its own rate
  talkers (1, 2, 3), 6 s; segSNR dB against the source, and the output
  level re the source in dB, both heard at 64 kHz; m = 64k / DNVT rate

                                        32k  level        16k  level
  the DNVT alone                       16.7   -0.5       10.8   -0.9    reference: its own codec, end to end
  up: repeat each bit                   5.4   +7.8        1.4  +16.5    DNVT -> trunk, into the 64k card as specified
  up: repeat, window x m               15.3   +0.6        9.7   +4.0    ... into a 64k decoder whose window is 3m bits
  up: tandem                           16.2   -0.7       10.8   -1.0    ... decoded and re-encoded on the card
  down: every m-th bit                  0.0  +58.7        0.0  +54.8    trunk -> DNVT, decimated
  down: remod                          16.6   -3.1        9.4   -8.6    ... summed per group, re-modulated to one bit
  down: tandem                         15.6   -0.6       10.8   -1.0    ... decoded and re-encoded on the card
  DNVT - 64k - DNVT, 2 tandems         15.1   -0.9       10.4   -1.0    two DNVTs through two transcoding cards

  Why decimation cannot work: the 64k encoder's bits in one 16k period
    net step  -4:  1.5 %  -2: 13.7 %  +0: 69.0 %  +2: 14.8 %  +4:  1.0 %
    the kept bit reports +-4 for every group; 69 % of groups moved 0.
    silence, 101010101010..., decimated 2:1 or 4:1 is 111111111111...: the far integrator goes to the rail.
  Why repetition fails into the card as specified: the integrator is exact
  (the same current for the same time), but a 3-bit window at 64k fires on
  the DNVT's runs of 2 at 32k and of 1 at 16k -- the step runs high.
  Repetition IS exact as transport: a card whose codec is clocked at the
  DNVT's rate, carrying each bit m times in the DS0, takes any one of each m
  back: bit-exact at every one of the 4 phases at 16k: True.

